```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!("Digest {}: {}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        let notified = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published: notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not add `aap:caps/http-client`. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and the graph is the authority for what a node may import. An unlisted import would give this body network access the graph does not declare. The enrichment call would also send the digest text to an external host, which should be reviewed explicitly. Once the graph definition includes the http-client grant, I can add the import and the enrichment call.

